WEBVTT

NOTE Unofficial English translation of the Thai narration. If it differs from the Thai original documents, the Thai original prevails.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:05.556
The Subcommittee on Military Affairs,
under the Senate Committee on

00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:09.679
Military Affairs and State
Security, held Meeting No. 31/2569.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:15.180
Wednesday, 11 November 2026,
at 9.00 a.m.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:20.640
Committee meeting room CA 321,
3rd floor, Parliament House.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:26.999
The subcommittee chair is
Asst. Prof. Nifarid Raden Ahmad.

00:00:27.079 --> 00:00:31.129
This subcommittee is part of the
Senate Committee on Military

00:00:31.129 --> 00:00:34.979
Affairs and State Security,
chaired by Mr. Somboon Nunual.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.880
The southern border provinces.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.009
Proposals on resolving the
unrest, the drug problem

00:00:41.009 --> 00:00:43.579
and building a
Thai–Malaysian border fence.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:47.853
The meeting agreed to pass
them to its working group

00:00:47.853 --> 00:00:52.288
that prepares policy proposals
for peace, public safety

00:00:52.288 --> 00:00:56.239
and development in the
southern border provinces.

00:00:56.321 --> 00:01:00.698
As for proposals on recovery,
remedies and lasting

00:01:00.698 --> 00:01:04.200
peace for people affected by the unrest,

00:01:04.281 --> 00:01:08.694
the approach is to gather initial
information from the petitioners

00:01:08.694 --> 00:01:12.439
and the agencies concerned,
to put before the committee.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.960
Complaints from the Senators Meet the
People project, lower southern group,

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:24.450
received during the field visit to
Narathiwat, Pattani and Yala in June.

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:27.272
They include a matter about
people taking part in national

00:01:27.272 --> 00:01:29.399
development in the
southern border provinces.

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:33.032
The meeting asked Working
Group 4 to gather information

00:01:33.032 --> 00:01:35.099
and look into the initial facts.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.200
Work related to the committee.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:44.360
The study report on using reserve
forces to support disaster relief

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:49.533
will go to the Senate in late
November or early December.

00:01:49.614 --> 00:01:56.043
The meeting considered the schedule of
a study visit on developing military

00:01:56.043 --> 00:02:01.700
and security capacity, on 25–26
November in Lop Buri and Saraburi.

00:02:01.781 --> 00:02:05.935
And it agreed to invite eight
agencies, plus the Civil

00:02:05.935 --> 00:02:09.550
Affairs Department, to
brief it on preparing to

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:13.319
prevent disaster crises
caused by global warming.

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.620
This will be put to the
committee for approval.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:20.500
The work of the four working groups.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.895
Working Group 1, on armed
forces structure, noted

00:02:23.895 --> 00:02:27.210
the issues of unrest, drugs
and the border fence.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:32.818
Working Group 2, on reserve forces,
reported on an academic seminar

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:37.768
on the transition to a new
reserve force development system,

00:02:37.768 --> 00:02:42.718
on 19 January 2027, to be put
to the committee for approval.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.653
Working Group 3 had no report.

00:02:44.733 --> 00:02:49.908
And Working Group 4, on law and
special affairs, noted proposals

00:02:49.908 --> 00:02:54.679
on amending security laws in
the southern border provinces.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.960
In the last six months, up to this
meeting, the subcommittee met 17 times.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.360
Next meeting: Wednesday,
18 November 2026, at 9.00 a.m.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.400
Committee meeting room
CA 321, 3rd floor.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.855
This summary is based
on the subcommittee's

00:03:14.855 --> 00:03:16.339
published meeting summary.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.411
Meeting minutes and reports
are available through

00:03:19.411 --> 00:03:22.219
the channels of the
Secretariat of the Senate.

